From d77a9f1a7539d6b5e8fc6a242f4f686f38579e2a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 03:54:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 07/40] dts: exynos: add the Exynos9820 and Galaxy S10+ device
 trees

Copies of the device trees this SoC and this phone have in the kernel,
which is what dts/upstream holds for every other board here. They are not
in the upstream collection yet, because the Linux side of this port has not
landed, so they arrive as a copy that the next sync will replace with the
real thing.

The files are byte for byte what the kernel series carries: the SoC tree
with its processors, timer, power management unit, clock controllers,
serial console and display pipeline, the pin controller tree with all eight
controllers and sixty two banks, and the board tree with its six memory
banks, which were read off the phone rather than guessed.

Nothing in them is specific to a boot loader. What this board needs on top
of them rides in its own file, as it does for the other phones here.

Signed-off-by: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
---
